Subject: [PATCH 4/5] hw/display/ati: vgpu3d Phase 3–5 — Metal dispatch thread
 scaffold

STATUS: STUB — not yet implemented.  This patch wires up the eventfd
doorbell, creates the Metal dispatch thread skeleton, and adds proper
lifecycle (start/join/cleanup).  The actual Metal API calls in the
thread body are left as annotated TODOs for Phase 5.

--- WHAT THIS PATCH ADDS ---

Phase 3 (command processor) and Phase 5 (Metal backend) share the same
host-thread infrastructure.  This patch establishes that infrastructure:

  1. EventNotifier  — replaces the (void)s doorbell stub from Phase 2.
     The guest writes VGPU3D_REG_DOORBELL → ati_vgpu3d_ctrl_write →
     event_notifier_set() → file-descriptor readable.

  2. ati_vgpu3d_thread — dedicated POSIX thread (QemuThread, joinable).
     Blocks on select(eventfd) so it consumes zero CPU when idle.
     The drain loop skeleton (ring_tail != ring_head) is present as a
     comment block ready for the Metal encoder calls in Phase 5.

  3. ati_vga_exit cleanup — stops the thread cleanly before device
     teardown to prevent use-after-free of the ring buffer mmap.

--- PHASE 5 IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE ---

Inside ati_vgpu3d_thread replace the TODO block with:

  while (s->vgpu3d.ring_tail != s->vgpu3d.ring_head) {
      Vgpu3dPacketHdr *hdr = ring_ptr(s, s->vgpu3d.ring_tail);
      switch (hdr->type) {
      case VGPU3D_PKT_DRAW_PRIMITIVE:  metal_draw_primitive(s, hdr); break;
      case VGPU3D_PKT_UPDATE_TEXTURE:  metal_update_texture(s, hdr);  break;
      /* ... */
      }
      s->vgpu3d.ring_tail =
          (s->vgpu3d.ring_tail + hdr->size) % VGPU3D_RING_DATA_SIZE;
      atomic_store(&s->vgpu3d.ring_tail, s->vgpu3d.ring_tail);
  }

The Metal encoder itself belongs in a new file hw/display/ati_metal.m
(Objective-C / Metal Shading Language) compiled only on Darwin targets.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Castelló <bfcastello@gmail.com>
